7:13:14Z"},"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-03-04T16:00:30Z","updated_at":"2025-03-05T18:08:53Z","closed_at":"2025-03-05T18:08:51Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.3 .Net\nGodot 4.4 .Net\n\n### System information\n\nWin10 22H2 x64\nRTX 3070, Driver 572.60\n\n### Issue description\nClicking any setting in the Material Inspector Panel, then clicking anything else in the Material Inspector Panel causes the panel to scroll down by a large amount. This becomes more annoying if the Inspector Panel is made smaller.\n\nIssue occurs in Normal Mode, in Self Contained Mode, and even after setting layout to default.\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/io/data_paths.html#self-contained-mode\n\nIssue does NOT occur if the Inspector Panel is Floating.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1) Add any node that supports a material, then add a material to the node. For example, add CSGBox with a StandardMaterial3D.\n2) Click on the StandardMaterial to view its properties in the Inspector Panel.\n3) Open up any section in the Material Inspector Panel. For example, I will open up Transparency.\n4) Click on any dropdown within Transparency. For example, Cull Mode's dropdown. Close the dropdown by selecting a dropdown option, or clicking outside the dropdown.\n5) Click again anywhere in the Material Inspector Panel that is NOT a setting. For example, click on the actual word \"Cull Mode\". This will trigger the bug -> The inspector scrolls down by a large amount.\n6) This may not seem like a big deal, but let's say you want to change Cull Mode's dropdown, and then the Albedo settings.\nYou click the Cull Mode dropdown and choose your setting. You then scroll down to click on Albedo section to expand it. Clicking on Albedo section will cause the inspector to scroll down by a large amount, forcing the user to scroll back up to Albedo.\n\nPerform the above with a floating Inspector Panel, and the bug will not occur.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103578/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103578/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}